o resist racking", "type": "fact"}]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE ale_id = 'ALE-STRC-005-02';
UPDATE public.taxonomy_tree SET wiki_items = '[{"text": "Definition: Application of compressive stress to concrete before loading", "type": "definition"}, {"text": "Purpose: Counteracts tensile stresses from loads", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Benefit: Allows longer spans, reduced deflection, cracks controlled", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Method: Tensioning tendons before concrete hardens (pretensioning)", "type": "concept"}, {"text": "Application: Precast members (beams, piles, planks)", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Transfer: Bond transfers compression as concrete cures", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Strengths: Very efficient for standard precast products", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Method: Tendons tensioned after concrete reaches strength", "type": "concept"}, {"text": "Ducts: Metal or plastic tubes in concrete for tendon routing", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Grouting: Tendons grouted after tensioning for long-term protection", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Can be applied after casting/assembly", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Allows curved tendon profiles", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Useful for large cast-in-place structures", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Long-span slabs", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Suspended slabs (cantilevers)", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Bridge decks", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Large buildings", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Initial Stress: Often eliminates tension, reduces cracks", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Prestress Loss: Immediate (elastic shortening, friction) and long-term (creep, shrinkage)", "type": "fact"}, {"text": "Strength Design: Reduced stress at ultimate (prestress force decreases as tendons stretch)", "type": "fact"}]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE ale_id = 'ALE-STRC-005-03';
